on Netflix is Wednesday the lead  character has a couple of boys clamoring  for her attention Jenna Ortega has some  thoughts about it and they're not what  you expect Jenna Ortega tackles the  iconic role of Wednesday Adams in  Wednesday a series that's broken  viewership records at Netflix while the  series pays homage to the characters  fans know and love from The Adams Family  but also includes new elements that add  to their backstory in this adaptation  Wednesday is a troubled teen headed for  Nevermore Academy Gomez and morticia's  alma mater that offers shelter to all  manner of monsters and outcasts  Wednesday is shown to be sardonic  quick-weighted and mischievous traits  that lead her to get wrapped up in a  mystery that threatens the lives of the  students at Nevermore even though she's  busy investigating Wednesday still has  time for a little romance after arriving  at her new school Wednesday quickly  finds two boys clamoring for her  attention there's a local teen named  Tyler The Helpful son of the town  sheriff and Xavier another Nevermore  student with strange Powers romance is a  common subplot in teen drama so it's not  all that surprising to see a love  triangle in the story however Ortega  isn't too fond of her character taking  part in such a cliche Trope throughout  season 1 of the series there's a monster  lurking in the woods surrounding  Nevermore Academy so naturally Wednesday  becomes determined to find out what's  going on the minds behind Wednesday  clearly wanted to keep the audience on  their toes because even as the boys try  to endear themselves to Wednesday it  becomes clear that either Tyler or  Xavier could be the culprit behind the  violent attacks that had been plaguing  the community however the love triangle  doesn't last by the end of the season  it's revealed that Tyler is the monster  effectively eliminating him as a  romantic interest or so it seems in any  case Jenna Ortega wasn't the biggest fan  of the storyline during an appearance on  the Canadian entertainment show e-talk  Ortega revealed that she wants to avoid  any more love triangles for Wednesday in  the future the actor explained well as  far as the boys went  I had to accept it Ortega then added  honestly I'm going to fight this love  triangle thing so hard because this is  just me being protective I don't think  Wednesday would ever be in a love  triangle even if you enjoyed Wednesday's  interactions with Tyler and Xavier  Ortega makes a good point there are  plenty of ways the series could develop  Wednesday's character without bringing  any Superfluous romance into the picture  in a Reddit thread criticizing  Wednesdays being nothing special one  Reddit user shared that like Ortega  they're not a fan of the season one love  triangle between Wednesday Tyler and  Xavier they wrote not every female  protagonist needs a love triangle or a  love interest for that matter I'm not an  anti-shipper or anything like that but  none of the love interest presented on  the show were likable or interesting to  me in response a number of commenters  either agreed outright or supported a  romance between Wednesday and her  roommate Enid as the only acceptable  option as the series continues even for  viewers who might have enjoyed  Wednesday's interactions with Tyler and  Xavier Ortega and her characters fans  all make a fair point there are plenty  of ways a series could develop  Wednesday's character without bringing  any superflu us romance into the picture  hopefully the writers take Ortega's  thoughts on love triangles into account  and lean into Wednesday's dark side if  the show gets a second season  [Music]
 

